.\" kpxcctl.1 — Man page for the KeePassXC Daemon CLI client
.TH KPXCTL 1 "2026-05-18" "kpxcd" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
kpxcctl \- command-line client for the KeePassXC daemon

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kpxcctl
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGUMENTS\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kpxcctl
is the command-line interface to \fBkpxcd\fR(8), the KeePassXC headless daemon.
It communicates with the daemon over the D-Bus session bus to manage databases,
retrieve entries, perform SSH operations, and manage local passkeys.

All operations require that \fBkpxcd\fR is running and reachable on the D-Bus
session bus.

.SH COMMANDS
.SS unlock
Unlock a KeePass database.

.nf
.B kpxcctl unlock <path>
.fi

Prompts for the database password on stdin. The database is then held in
memory by the daemon until explicitly locked or until the idle timeout expires.

.SS lock
Lock a database or all databases.

.nf
.B kpxcctl lock [uuid|all]
.fi

If no argument or \fBall\fR is given, all unlocked databases are locked.
If a UUID is given, only that database is locked. Decrypted data is wiped
from memory using secure zeroing.

.SS list
List all known databases and their lock status.

.nf
.B kpxcctl list [--json]
.fi

Displays a table of UUID, name, lock status, and path. Use \fB\-\-json\fR
for machine-readable output.

.SS get
Retrieve fields for a specific entry.

.nf
.B kpxcctl get <uuid> <entry-path>
.fi

The entry path is a slash-separated path from the root group, e.g.,
\fI/General/example.com\fR. Displays safe metadata fields: title, username,
and URL. It does not return passwords, notes, or TOTP codes.

.SS ssh
Manage SSH keys stored in KeePass databases and served by the agent.

.TP
.B kpxcctl ssh list [uuid]
List SSH keys loaded in the agent. Optionally filter by database UUID.

.TP
.B kpxcctl ssh add <uuid> <entry-path>
Add an SSH key from the specified database entry to the agent.

.TP
.B kpxcctl ssh remove <fingerprint>
Remove an SSH key from the agent by its SHA256 fingerprint.

.TP
.B kpxcctl ssh scan [uuid]
Scan unlocked database(s) for entries containing SSH keys.
Shows entry UUID, title, key type, and fingerprint.

.TP
.B kpxcctl ssh show <fingerprint>
Show metadata for a loaded SSH key.

.TP
.B kpxcctl ssh generate <uuid> <entry-path> [\-\-type rsa|ed25519|ecdsa] [\-\-bits N] [\-\-comment text]
Generate a new SSH key pair, store the private key as an attachment in the
specified entry, and set KeeAgent metadata. The public key is not stored
separately; it can be derived from the private key attachment.

.TP
.B kpxcctl ssh import
Show a menu of private keys found in ~/.ssh and import the selected ones.
Skips keys already stored (matched by fingerprint) and unsupported sk-* keys.
.TP
.B kpxcctl ssh autoload
Show a menu of the database's keys and toggle which auto-load at unlock.
.TP
.B kpxcctl ssh autoload <uuid> <entry> on|off [\-\-override-deny]
Set or clear auto-load for one entry (writes the KPXCD_SSH_KEY marker and
KeeAgent.settings). Applies at next unlock.
.TP
.B kpxcctl ssh import <uuid> <entry-path> <file> [\-\-delete-after]
Import an existing SSH private key into the database. The key file is
read, parsed, attached to the entry, and KeeAgent metadata is set.
With \fB\-\-delete-after\fR, the source file is removed after successful import.

.TP
.B kpxcctl ssh export
Show a menu of stored keys and export one (polkit-gated).
.TP
.B kpxcctl ssh export <uuid> <entry> <file> [\-\-force] [\-\-no-passphrase]
Export one stored key to OpenSSH format. Gated by polkit auth_self per call.
Output is created 0600 with O_EXCL (never stdout), encrypted with a passphrase
unless --no-passphrase.
Export is polkit-gated (auth_self per call); output is 0600 and never stdout.

.TP
.B kpxcctl ssh diag
Print SSH agent diagnostics: mode, socket path, and loaded key summary.

.SS passkey
Local passkey management, available when the FIDO2 service is enabled.
Mutations require authorization. These commands do not register a key with a site.

.TP
.B kpxcctl passkey list
List stored passkey metadata.
.TP
.B kpxcctl passkey create <uuid> <rpID> <username> [displayName]
Create an append-only local credential with a generated handle. Browser native
registration instead preserves the RP-supplied user ID.
.TP
.B kpxcctl passkey remove <credentialID>
Remove a stored credential. Obtain approval and a recovery path before deletion.
.TP
.B kpxcctl passkey import <uuid> <bitwarden.json> [\-\-dry-run] [\-\-all | \-\-rp=<rpID> | \-\-cred=<credentialID>]
Import selected ECDSA P-256 credentials from a decrypted Bitwarden export.
Protect the export as private key material. Local import cannot change original
server/browser transport hints excluding USB. Import/account changes require
separate approval.
.PP
There is no passkey assert CLI command. The implemented D-Bus AssertPasskey method
accepts a caller-supplied hash and uses a separate polkit path; do not infer native
UHID cancellation or UV guarantees for it. See doc/passkeys.md.

.SS ping
Check whether the daemon is running and responsive.

.nf
.B kpxcctl doctor <old.kdbx>
Diagnose an old database read-only: legacy passkey field names, missing
backup-flag fields, legacy KeeAgent custom data, unmarked SSH key
attachments, KDBX version. Exits 2 when fixable issues are found.
.TP
.B kpxcctl doctor --fix <old.kdbx> <new.kdbx>
Create a FRESH vault at <new.kdbx> (new MasterSeed/EncryptionIV/inner stream
key, so old synced/backup versions can no longer be XOR-combined), with all
entries copied and legacy metadata migrated to KeePassXC-compatible form.
The old file is never modified; <new.kdbx> must not exist. Prompts for the
old password and a new one (enter keeps the old). Output is 0600.
.TP
.B kpxcctl ping
.fi

Prints \fIpong\fR if the daemon is alive. Exits with an error otherwise.

.SS help
Print usage information.

.SH OPTIONS
.B kpxcctl
does not accept global options. Each command may have its own flags (e.g.,
\fB\-\-json\fR for \fBlist\fR). Use \fBkpxcctl help\fR for command-specific
help.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS
D-Bus session bus address. If not set, the default session bus is used.
\fBkpxcctl\fR must be able to reach the same session bus as \fBkpxcd\fR.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B Unlock a database:
.nf
    kpxcctl unlock ~/Passwords.kdbx
.fi

.TP
.B Lock all databases:
.nf
    kpxcctl lock all
.fi

.TP
.B List databases in JSON format:
.nf
    kpxcctl list --json
.fi

.TP
.B Retrieve an entry:
.nf
    kpxcctl get abc123 /General/github.com
.fi

.TP
.B List SSH keys:
.nf
    kpxcctl ssh list
.fi

.TP
.B Check daemon status:
.nf
    kpxcctl ping
.fi

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kpxcd (8),
.BR kpxcd.toml (5),
